# Kernel modules RoboDR's enforcing units need, loaded at boot by
# systemd-modules-load. Example (installed as
# /usr/share/doc/robodr/examples/modules-load.d/robodr.conf.example, never
# active). Install only the part for the units you enable:
#
#   install -m 0644 robodr.conf.example /etc/modules-load.d/robodr.conf
#
# Why preload: robodr-executor runs with ProtectKernelModules=yes and only
# CAP_NET_ADMIN, so it cannot load a module itself, and the first
# containment on a host where nf_tables was never used would otherwise
# depend on the kernel's on-demand loading. `robodr-setup preflight`
# reports whether nf_tables is loaded, built in or available.
#
# Detection alone (robodr-agentd, robodr-pulsard) needs none of these.

# --- robodr-executor (isolate_network, quarantine_node): table inet robodr
nf_tables

# --- robodr-firewall-gw (inline gateway on a sensor box; see its README,
# "Kernel requirements"). robodr-firewall-gw-rules.service loads
# br_netfilter itself; preloading makes a missing module fail at boot, not
# at the first start of the gateway. Uncomment on a gateway box only.
#br_netfilter
#nfnetlink_queue
#nfnetlink_log
#xt_NFQUEUE
#xt_NFLOG
#xt_physdev
